## P1: Core Capability and Admin UX

### P1.1 Admin panel sub-menu architecture
- Source: Items 5 and 6
- Requirement:
	- Admin tools must be split into distinct sub-menus/views:
		- Edit Users
		- Create User
		- Audit
	- Each tool has isolated local state and clear navigation.
- Why now: Reduces operator errors and supports scaling admin features.
- Dependencies: P0.4 recommended first (permissions affect visible tools)
- Done when:
	- Admin sees discrete sub-menu entries for each tool.
	- Tool content does not overlap in a shared conflicting form state.

### P1.2 Fix Create User/Edit User state coupling bug
- Source: Item 7
- Requirement:
	- Creating a user must use a separate form model from edit user.
	- Edits in Create User cannot mutate Edit User in-memory state.
- Why now: Current behavior risks incorrect account changes.
- Dependencies: P1.1 (or fix in parallel by splitting state stores)
- Done when:
	- Repro no longer occurs.
	- Unit/integration tests protect against cross-form state bleed.

### P1.3 Workspace creation support
- Source: Item 4
- Requirement:
	- Add ability to create a new workspace from UI.
	- Newly created workspace is persisted and selectable immediately.
	- Sample workspaces are optional, not required for operation.
- Why now: Core product functionality currently missing.
- Dependencies: P0.1 (fresh data baseline), P0.4 (permissions for who can create)
- Done when:
	- User with proper permission can create, view, and interact with a new workspace.

